{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e05eea0-3c6c-4928-a22d-8bf3f8a40a67",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 10. HTTP ENTITY\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c2988fd-82cc-4779-aa49-24523d01eea4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In older HTTP/1.1 terminology, an ENTITY refers to the\n",
    "information/content transferred in an HTTP request or response.\n",
    "\n",
    "An entity consists of:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Entity\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- Entity Headers\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- Entity Body\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "04514328-5c45-4742-96f7-497aceb9b5f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "1. ENTITY HEADER\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity headers provide metadata about the entity body.\n",
    "\n",
    "Metadata means:\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Information ABOUT the actual data.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Type: application/json\n",
    "Content-Length: 45\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Type\n",
    "    → tells what type of data is present\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Length\n",
    "    → tells how much data is present\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "9be66e14-cde8-443a-93c4-6d29958b21b3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "2. ENTITY BODY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "The entity body contains the actual data/content.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "POST /users HTTP/1.1\n",
    "Content-Type: application/json\n",
    "Content-Length: 35\n",
    "\n",
    "{\n",
    "  \"name\": \"Mayuri\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "Headers\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "Describe the data\n",
    "\n",
    "Body\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "Contains the actual data\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "1c44cce0-a19b-412b-acd9-1fb4d97371c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "3. SIMPLE EXAMPLE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Consider:\n",
    "\n",
    "HTTP/1.1 200 OK\n",
    "Content-Type: text/html\n",
    "Content-Length: 40\n",
    "\n",
    "<html>\n",
    "<body>Hello</body>\n",
    "</html>\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity Headers:\n",
    "    Content-Type: text/html\n",
    "    Content-Length: 40\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity Body:\n",
    "    <html>\n",
    "    <body>Hello</body>\n",
    "    </html>\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of it as:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Entity\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +-------------------+\n",
    "       |                   |\n",
    "       ↓                   ↓\n",
    "   Metadata             Actual Data\n",
    "       |                   |\n",
    "       ↓                   ↓\n",
    "Content-Type          HTML content\n",
    "Content-Length"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "78d92e64-8c87-4aa5-92f4-fe450ae8d717",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "4. ENTITY WITHOUT A BODY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Sometimes an HTTP response may contain headers but\n",
    "no entity body.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "HTTP/1.1 200 OK\n",
    "Content-Type: text/html\n",
    "Content-Length: 100\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "There is no actual body in this message.\n",
    "\n",
    "The headers can still provide information about the\n",
    "resource/content.\n",
    "\n",
    "A common example is the HEAD method.\n",
    "\n",
    "HEAD asks the server for information about a resource\n",
    "without requesting the actual response body.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "HEAD /index.html HTTP/1.1\n",
    "Host: example.com\n",
    "\n",
    "The server can return headers such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Type: text/html\n",
    "Content-Length: 5000\n",
    "\n",
    "but does not send the HTML body.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "5c616fd5-2b88-4c56-a1e0-fcddf33b1434",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "5. ENTITY HEADERS vs ENTITY BODY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "ENTITY HEADERS\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Describe the data\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Type\n",
    "Content-Length\n",
    "Content-Encoding\n",
    "Last-Modified\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ENTITY BODY\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains the actual data\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "JSON\n",
    "HTML\n",
    "XML\n",
    "Text\n",
    "Image\n",
    "File"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "829111d1-2572-46d8-b928-6c0427d97768",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "5. ENTITY HEADERS vs ENTITY BODY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "ENTITY HEADERS\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Describe the data\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Type\n",
    "Content-Length\n",
    "Content-Encoding\n",
    "Last-Modified\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ENTITY BODY\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains the actual data\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "JSON\n",
    "HTML\n",
    "XML\n",
    "Text\n",
    "Image\n",
    "File\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "6. COMPLETE HTTP EXAMPLE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Request:\n",
    "\n",
    "POST /users HTTP/1.1\n",
    "Host: example.com\n",
    "Content-Type: application/json\n",
    "Content-Length: 35\n",
    "\n",
    "{\n",
    "  \"name\": \"Mayuri\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity headers:\n",
    "    Content-Type: application/json\n",
    "    Content-Length: 35\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity body:\n",
    "    {\n",
    "      \"name\": \"Mayuri\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Server processes the entity body and may send:\n",
    "\n",
    "HTTP/1.1 201 Created\n",
    "Content-Type: application/json\n",
    "\n",
    "{\n",
    "  \"id\": 101,\n",
    "  \"name\": \"Mayuri\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "The response also contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Headers\n",
    "       +\n",
    "    Body\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "7. IMPORTANT: ENTITY IS OLD TERMINOLOGY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Entity\" is terminology from older HTTP specifications,\n",
    "especially HTTP/1.1 RFC 2616.\n",
    "\n",
    "Modern HTTP specifications generally use terms such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Message\n",
    "    Content\n",
    "    Representation\n",
    "\n",
    "instead of treating \"entity\" as the main concept.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, if your syllabus uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Entity\n",
    "    Entity Header\n",
    "    Entity Body\n",
    "\n",
    "you should understand and write the older terminology\n",
    "for your exam.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "8. EASY WAY TO REMEMBER\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "ENTITY = DATA BEING TRANSFERRED\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity Headers\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "Tell us ABOUT the data\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity Body\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "Contains the ACTUAL data\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Content-Type: application/json\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "\"What type of data?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "{\n",
    "  \"name\": \"Mayuri\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "\"What is the actual data?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "SUMMARY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "HTTP Entity consists of:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Entity\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- Entity Headers\n",
    "       |       ↓\n",
    "       |    Metadata about the data\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- Entity Body\n",
    "               ↓\n",
    "            Actual data\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Key idea:\n",
    "\n",
    "HEADER → describes the data\n",
    "BODY   → contains the data\n",
    "\n",
    "Note:\n",
    "\"Entity\" and \"Entity Header\" are older HTTP terminology,\n",
    "but they are still commonly found in HTTP/1.1 textbooks\n",
    "and syllabi."
   ]
  },
